{
    "reasoner_response": "Begin by acknowledging the customer's vehicle: "I see you have a 2022 FORD EXPLORER XLT." Then explain: "Based on your contract terms, engine repairs are not covered under your contract. This contract is a maintenance agreement, which covers services like oil changes, tire rotations, and multipoint inspections performed by your selling dealer or its affiliate. It does not cover mechanical breakdowns or repairs to your engine." Add: "Please keep in mind that the actual coverage available to you will depend on your specific claim's authorization." Ask if there is anything else the customer would like help with.",
    "communication_rules": [
        "- If the customer tried to change the topic while you are waiting for Supervisor instructions, before following any Reasoner's instructions, ask the customer whether they want to switch to the new topic or continue with the current one.",
        "- If any previous requests were prevented from execution, they can now be re-evaluated and executed if appropriate. Make a new function/tool request to do so."
    ]
}
